# guard for 2.2.2.gather-experiences
#
# the citation gate. every gathered case must trace to a bhrowser read, spread across
# sources, with the comments read. a wrong citation here poisons the disentangle downstream
# and, in a medical registry, can carry into guidance a human acts on. the bar is absolute.

artifacts:
  - $route/2.2.2.gather-experiences.yield.md

reviews:
  self:
    - slug: has-bhrowser-citations
      say: |
        every case must trace to a bhrowser read — never WebSearch or WebFetch.

        for each case, check:
        - is there a source url?
        - is there a verbatim quote from what the bhrowser returned?
        - could a reader re-open that url and find the same text?

        if any case lacks a bhrowser-verified url + verbatim quote, it is a blocker.
        (rule.require.bhrowser-citations)

    - slug: has-comments-read
      say: |
        social posts are signal, not fact — the comments carry the correction.

        for each social thread, check:
        - were the replies read and captured, not just the original post?
        - did a reply contradict, qualify, or confirm the post? is that recorded?

        an original post saved without its comments is a blocker.
        (rule.require.read-social-comments)

    - slug: has-source-spread
      say: |
        do not lean on one subreddit — r/AskVet auto-strips anecdotes.

        are the cases spread across multiple sources
        (r/cats, r/CatAdvice, r/Pets, vet forums), not a single well?

    - slug: has-bias-recorded
      say: |
        the sample skews to problems — people post when a pet suffers, rarely when it is fine.

        is that selection bias recorded here, so the downstream stats carry it forward
        as an upper bound, not a base rate?

  peer:
    - $rhachet run --repo bhrain --skill review --brain anthropic/claude/code/haiku --rules '.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/rule.require.{bhrowser-citations,read-social-comments,source-inventory,seven-distinct-citations}.*.md' --paths '$route/2.2.2.gather-experiences.yield.md' --output '$route/.reviews/$stone.peer-review.citations.md'
    # citation-count reviewer — the deepseek l1 rule (rule.require.fifty-divergent-citations).
    # NOTE: fireworks/deepseek/v4-flash is the preferred brain but is not registered here; and
    # xai/grok atoms fault in this env (supplier.creds is not a function). the proven-working
    # provider is anthropic/claude/code, so a DISTINCT anthropic brain (sonnet, separate from the
    # haiku citations reviewer above) enforces the count rule as an independent second l1.
    # once the fireworks provider + FIREWORKS_API_KEY are wired, swap this back to deepseek.
    - $rhachet run --repo bhrain --skill review --brain anthropic/claude/code/sonnet --rules '.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/rule.require.{fifty-divergent-citations,bhrowser-citations}.*.md' --paths '$route/2.2.2.gather-experiences.yield.md' --output '$route/.reviews/$stone.peer-review.citation-count.md'

judges:
  - rhx route.stone.judge --mechanism reviewed? --stone $stone --route $route --allow-blockers 0 --allow-nitpicks 3
